<http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00011565> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                  owl:versionIRI <http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00011565> ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/conforms_to_gpad> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/modelstate> "production" ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8769-177X" ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date> "2026-10-26"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "REG3G-EXTL3 signalling suppresses the kynurenine pathway and protects HK1-dependent glycolysis (Human)"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/pav/providedBy> "http://geneontology.org"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "Curated with GO AI HUB. Human counterpart of gomodel:6ab067da00011397: REG3G-EXTL3 signalling suppresses the kynurenine pathway and protects HK1-dependent glycolysis."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Human counterpart of mouse model gomodel:6ab067da00011397, same structure. Facts resting on mouse data from PMID:35263589 are ISS (GO_REF:0000024) with the mouse gene; where the mouse model used ISS from a human ortholog, this model cites that human experimental evidence directly. Microglial and neuronal context is ISS from mouse."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Quinolinate (CHEBI:29959) is not the direct product of any activity in this model. HAAO outputs cis,cis-2-amino-3-carboxymuconate 6-semialdehyde (CHEBI:77612, RHEA:17953), which cyclises to quinolinate spontaneously. There is no enzyme and therefore no activity unit for that step; the quinolinate node represents its product, and the HAAO -> SRC causal edge carries the biology."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "XIAP is modelled with signaling adaptor activity (GO:0035591), transferred by ISS from mouse Xiap. The underlying mouse data (PMID:35263589 Fig. 6C binding, Fig. 6D knockdown) do not establish which function XIAP performs; XIAP's established MF is E3 ubiquitin ligase activity, untested in this pathway."^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <https://w3id.org/biolink/vocab/in_taxon> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606> .

